  "reviewed_interpretation": "The single authoritative I039 execution is valid and terminal. All preregistered dataset, fresh-seed, causal coverage, fixed-horizon, exact-order bitwise reconstruction, post-NS partition-accounting, suppression-transfer invariant and shipping-mirror gates passed. The fixed shipping suppression transfer explains part of the response mismatch in the fixed speech domain: across horizons 1/2/4/8 the median predicted-suppressed versus actual post-NS alignment error is about 6.17/4.90/4.68/4.53 dB, smaller than the corresponding tracker-versus-post-NS error of about 10.31/9.42/7.37/6.71 dB, while the predicted/post response-magnitude ratio rises from about 0.67 to 0.85. However a substantial residual remains. In the all domain the predicted-versus-post median alignment error remains about 4.34-5.62 dB and is not consistently better than tracker-versus-post. Therefore instantaneous suppression gain alone is not a complete mechanism for the matched-domain mismatch. These observations remain diagnostic and do not select any domain, estimator, normalization, NS floor, suppression gain, alpha, threshold, horizon, lag, mapping, refresh rule or source candidate.",
